# Explicit Riemann/Darboux theorem: riemann_integrable_continuous.
# Check: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/stmt_nodes/release_and_expand/builtin_thm/riemann_integrable_continuous.lit
# The theorem checks its actual domain and all premises before publishing results.
have fn square(x R) R=x^2
release thm riemann_integrable_continuous(square,0,1)
integral(square,0,1)=integral(square,0,1)
# Existence permits a symbolic value; it does not identify that value as 1/3.
